<title>USA: US needs to pay off debts to World Bank - Clinton.</title>
<headline>US needs to pay off debts to World Bank - Clinton.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton declared on Tuesday that the United States needed to pay off its debts to the World Bank, the United Nations and other international institutions.</p>
<p>&quot;If America is to continue to lead the world, we here who lead America simply must find the will to pay our way,&quot; Clinton said in his prepared State of the Union address for delivery to Congress.  </p>
<p>The United States is $234.5 million behind in its payments to the World Bank's International Development Association affiliate, which lends money to very poor countries.</p>
<p>&quot;We must ... renew our commitment to America's diplomacy -- and pay our debts and dues to international financial institutions like the World Bank, and to a reforming United Nations,&quot; Clinton said.</p>
</text>
